{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/166943": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant/Program Administrator, School of Medicine",
      "description": "Executive Assistant/Program Administrator, School of Medicine You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Executive Assistant/Program Administrator, School of Medicine School of Medicine Location - Fayetteville, NC 28304 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description Methodist University seeks candidates for an Executive Assistant/Program Administrator, School of Medicine. There are two positions available: an Executive Assistant/Program Administrator for the Academic Affairs Office and an Executive Assistant/Program Administrator for the Student Experience Office within its new School of Medicine, established in partnership with Cape Fear Valley Health in Fayetteville, NC.  Reporting directly to the Chief of Staff of the Medical School, the Executive Assistant/Program Administrator will support the Senior Associate Dean and program team for either Academic Affairs or Student Experience by providing high-level administrative and operational support. The successful candidate will demonstrate exceptional organizational, communication, and time management skills while serving as a trusted partner to the Senior Associate Dean and the program team. Responsibilities include coordinating and managing complex schedules, supporting activities, preparing and organizing meeting agendas and minutes, and supporting committee operations. The ideal candidate will possess a growth mindset, pay attention to details, demonstrate adaptability in the face of evolving priorities, proactively identify opportunities for improvement, and contribute positively to a culture of continuous learning and excellence. A commitment to collaboration, professionalism, customer service, and student-centered support is essential. The ideal candidate will have three or more years of administrative experience in higher education and is committed to furthering the mission, vision, and goals of the College of Medicine and Methodist University. A bachelor's degree or higher is preferred. Interested applicants should apply through the Methodist University website. Provide high-level administrative and operational support to the Senior Associate Dean and the Academic Affairs Office/ or Student Experience Office. Coordinate and manage complex calendars, schedules, appointments, meetings, and special events for the Academic Affairs Office. Prepare, organize, and distribute meeting agendas, materials, minutes, and follow-up action items for committees, working groups, and leadership meetings. Assist with planning, coordinating, and supporting programs, events, activities, and initiatives. Prepare, proofread, edit, and distribute correspondence, reports, memoranda, presentations, forms, and other documents on behalf of Academic Affairs leadership. Research, compile, analyze, and organize information and data for reports, presentations, and meetings. Generate and prepare reports and supporting materials for internal and external meetings as requested. Maintain confidential records, files, databases, and documentation while exercising discretion and safeguarding sensitive information. Establish and maintain organized administrative, personnel, and office records, ensuring compliance with retention and purging procedures as appropriate. Support committee operations by coordinating logistics, maintaining records, tracking action items, and facilitating communication among committee members. Serve as a key point of contact for students, faculty, staff, and external stakeholders, providing exceptional customer service and professional support. Coordinate office logistics, including purchasing supplies and materials needed for Student Experience programs, events, and daily operations. Identify opportunities to improve workflows, processes, and administrative efficiency within the Academic Affairs Office. Manage multiple priorities simultaneously while meeting deadlines in a dynamic, fast-paced environment with frequent interruptions. Assist with special projects and assignments that advance the mission, vision, and goals of the School of Medicine and Methodist University. Support School of Medicine events, activities, and initiatives as needed, which may occasionally require attendance outside normal business hours, including evenings and weekends. Demonstrate professionalism, adaptability, sound judgment, attention to detail, and a commitment to continuous improvement in all aspects of the role. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Required experience: 3 years or more of administrative experience in higher education. Some college training in business related subjects (and/or Business College training) or a combination MS Office suite (Teams, Excel, Word, etc.) and virtual meeting platforms (WebEx, Zoom, Teams, etc) Preferred experience: Health profession education, student affairs management or similar. Bachelor’s degree or higher preferred Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/166835": {
      "title": "Police Officer (Part-Time)",
      "description": "Police Officer (Part-Time) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Police Officer (Part-Time) Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Salary Range $24.00 - $27.00 Hourly Position Type Part Time Staff Apply Description The below listed job announcement is for a position as a Police Officer on the Campus of Methodist University, located at 5400 Ramsey Street, Fayetteville, North Carolina.  We invite applicants to come join Methodist University as a Police Officer, a job that makes a difference in our campus community. Schedule and Pay: Hours per week can fluctuate based on department need, up to 24 hours a week maximum The schedule will be based on the needs of the department.  The position will primarily fill in for open shifts and provide staffing support during events Candidates must have a flexible schedule and be willing to accept shifts on short notice, including nights, weekends, and holidays. Pay Range: $24.00 - $27.00 an hour $3,000 Sign-On/Retention Bonus Minimal job description below – additional job functions as required by the North Carolina Department of Justice Criminal Justice Education and Training Standards Division. Police Officers support the mission, goals, and objectives of the University, the Division of Student Development and Services, and that of the Department of Public Safety. Specific duties and responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Enforcing State and Federal Laws; and local ordinances Protecting the Methodist University Community and Property (Students, Faculty, Staff and Guest) from criminal offenses committed in Methodist University Police Jurisdiction. Maintain proficiency in all essential job functions of a Law Enforcement Officer as indicated in Attachment V of the Criminal Justice Education and Training Standards Commission form (F-8) Securing campus facilities either by your presence or through the building security plan Following in detail the Public Safety Manual of procedures and any directives received from the Chief/Director or any supervisory staff within the Police Department. Respond to all law enforcement related calls for assistance within the Methodist University Jurisdiction. Assist in providing Police coverage on a 24 hour basis; and as directed by your supervisor. Communicate any Police problems/issues to your Police Supervisor. Responsible for the completion and filing of all forms; such as: Incident Reports Daily Patrol Reports Maintenance Reports Accident Reports (Personnel/Property) Other reports as required In addition, you are responsible to fulfill all rules, regulations, and guidelines of Methodist University; and to be a proper role model for students at all times. Finally, you are responsible for fulfilling other duties as assigned by the University President, Vice President of Student Development and Services, the Chief of Police/Director of Police and Public Safety, and any other Supervisor assigned to the Methodist University Police Department. Qualifications Minimum Education/Experience: High School Diploma or Equivalent Have successfully completed Basic Law Enforcement Training for the State of North Carolina Have at least one year of law enforcement Successful candidates must meet the following requirements: Pass an oral interview Meet all requirements of the commissioning process May be required to undergo additional screening test/exams as determined by the Chief of Police/Director of Police and Public Safety Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/166743": {
      "title": "Police Officer (Full-Time)",
      "description": "Police Officer (Full-Time) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Police Officer (Full-Time) Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Salary Range $24.00 - $27.00 Hourly Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description The below listed job announcement is for a position as a Police Officer on the Campus of Methodist University, located at 5400 Ramsey Street, Fayetteville, North Carolina. We invite applicants to come join Methodist University as a Police Officer, a job that makes a difference in our campus community. Schedule and Pay: 40 Hour Work Week: 4 Days a week, 10-hour shifts Permanent Shifts Pay Range: $24.00 - $27.00 an hour (Annual Salary Range: $49,920 - $56,160) $3,000 Sign-On/Retention Bonus Minimal job description below – additional job functions as required by the North Carolina Department of Justice Criminal Justice Education and Training Standards Division. Police Officers support the mission, goals, and objectives of the University, the Division of Student Development and Services, and that of the Department of Public Safety. Specific duties and responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Enforcing State and Federal Laws; and local ordinances Protecting the Methodist University Community and Property (Students, Faculty, Staff and Guest) from criminal offenses committed in Methodist University Police Jurisdiction. Maintain proficiency in all essential job functions of a Law Enforcement Officer as indicated in Attachment V of the Criminal Justice Education and Training Standards Commission form (F-8) Securing campus facilities either by your presence or through the building security plan Following in detail the Public Safety Manual of procedures and any directives received from the Chief/Director or any supervisory staff within the Police Department. Respond to all law enforcement related calls for assistance within the Methodist University Jurisdiction. Assist in providing Police coverage on a 24 hour basis; and as directed by your supervisor. Communicate any Police problems/issues to your Police Supervisor. Responsible for the completion and filing of all forms; such as: Incident Reports Daily Patrol Reports Maintenance Reports Accident Reports (Personnel/Property) Other reports as required In addition, you are responsible to fulfill all rules, regulations, and guidelines of Methodist University; and to be a proper role model for students at all times. Finally, you are responsible for fulfilling other duties as assigned by the University President, Vice President of Student Development and Services, the Chief of Police/Director of Police and Public Safety, and any other Supervisor assigned to the Methodist University Police Department. Qualifications Minimum Education/Experience: High School Diploma or Equivalent Have successfully completed Basic Law Enforcement Training for the State of North Carolina Have at least one year of law enforcement Successful candidates must meet the following requirements: Pass an oral interview Meet all requirements of the commissioning process May be required to undergo additional screening test/exams as determined by the Chief of Police/Director of Police and Public Safety Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
