    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/166597": {
      "title": "Assistant Director for Didactic and Simulation Education, Nurse Anesthesia Program",
      "description": "Assistant Director for Didactic and Simulation Education, Nurse Anesthesia Program You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Director for Didactic and Simulation Education, Nurse Anesthesia Program Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Faculty Apply Description Reports to: CRNA Program Director Position Summary: The primary responsibility of this position is leadership of the didactic and simulation curriculum of the Nurse Anesthesia Program. This includes course coordination, simulation lab education, and learner academic assessment. The position also includes classroom instruction and student advisement. The Assistant Director for Didactic and Simulation Education reports to the Program Director. This position works closely with the Assistant Director for Clinical Residency so that what learners gain in the classroom and simulation lab carries into clinical practice. Position Responsibilities Assist the Program Director to ensure compliance with the accreditation standards of the Council on Accreditation of Nurse Anesthesia Educational Programs (COA). Hold primary responsibility for standards related to curriculum, instruction, and learner assessment in the didactic and simulation components. Provide assistance with the administrative responsibilities of the program as assigned by the Program Director. Coordinate the didactic curriculum, including course sequencing, syllabi, faculty teaching assignments, and course evaluations. Provide instruction in core nurse anesthesia course content Lead development of the simulation curriculum. Map simulation experiences to course and clinical outcomes and use competency-based evaluation. Oversee nurse anesthesia simulation lab operations, including scheduling, equipment, and supplies. Coordinate use of shared simulation and educational resources across the university. Develop interprofessional simulation experiences with other health professions programs. Orient and develop didactic faculty, guest lecturers, and simulation facilitators. Oversee the design and quality of course examinations, including item analysis and test review. Monitor learner academic performance. Work collaboratively with the Program Director and faculty to provide counseling and assessment of remediation needs of learners. Prepare learners for the Self-Evaluation Examination (SEE) and the National Certification Examination (NCE). Track and report results. Coordinate research and evidence-based practice activities for learners and CRNA faculty, including DNP scholarly projects. Work with the Assistant Director for Clinical Residency so that course content and simulation prepare learners for clinical expectations at each stage of the program. Collect and report didactic and simulation outcome data for program evaluation and the COA annual report. Participate in preparation for the COA accreditation site visit. Serve on the Admissions Committee for review and selection of candidates for admission. Serve on the Curriculum Committee and provide leadership in curriculum development, assessment, and revision to meet COA and CCNE curriculum and learner outcome standards. Qualifications Required Qualifications Doctoral degree (PhD, EdD, or DNP) from an institution of higher education accredited by an agency recognized by the US Secretary of Education at the time the degree was conferred. Current unencumbered license, or eligibility for licensure, as a registered nurse and advanced practice registered nurse (APRN) in North Carolina. Current certification or recertification as a Certified Registered Nurse Anesthetist (CRNA) from the National Board of Certification and Recertification for Nurse Anesthetists (NBCRNA). Current Advanced Cardiac Life Support (ACLS) and Pediatric Advanced Life Support (PALS) certifications. Minimum of three years of clinical experience as a CRNA. Formal education in curriculum, instruction, and evaluation. Experience in simulation-based education. Preferred Qualifications Certified Healthcare Simulation Educator (CHSE) credential. Certified Nurse Educator (CNE) credential. Experience developing courses and examinations in a nurse anesthesia or graduate health professions program. Teaching and academic administrative experience. Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/166476": {
      "title": "Assistant Director for Clinical Education, Nurse Anesthesia Program",
      "description": "Assistant Director for Clinical Education, Nurse Anesthesia Program You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Director for Clinical Education, Nurse Anesthesia Program Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Faculty Apply Description Reports to: CRNA Program Director Position Summary: The primary responsibility of this position is leadership of the clinical portion of the Nurse Anesthesia Program. This includes clinical site development, learner clinical assignments, and clinical evaluation. The position also includes classroom instruction and student advisement. The Assistant Director for Clinical Education reports to the Program Director and performs the duties of the Program Director in their absence. This position works closely with the Assistant Director for Didactic and Simulation Education so that what learners gain in the classroom and simulation lab carries into clinical practice. Position Responsibilities Assist the Program Director to ensure compliance with the accreditation standards of the Council on Accreditation of Nurse Anesthesia Educational Programs (COA). Hold primary responsibility for standards related to clinical sites and clinical learning. Provide assistance with the administrative responsibilities of the program and assume the Program Director role in their absence. Develop and maintain clinical sites that provide the case volume and variety required by COA. This includes site recruitment, affiliation agreements, and annual site evaluation. Serve as the primary program liaison to clinical partners, including Clinical Site Coordinators and anesthesia department leaders. Coordinate learner clinical rotation assignments and schedules across all clinical sites. Monitor learner case and clinical hour records to confirm each learner is on track to meet COA graduation requirements. Oversee clinical evaluation, including preceptor evaluation of learners and learner evaluation of sites and preceptors. Conduct regular clinical site visits to observe learners and support preceptors. Orient and develop clinical preceptors and Clinical Site Coordinators. Work collaboratively with the Program Director and faculty to identify learners who need clinical remediation. Develop and monitor remediation plans. Ensure learners complete clinical onboarding requirements, such as credentialing, immunizations, background checks, and drug screening. Work with the Assistant Director for Didactic and Simulation Education so that course content and simulation prepare learners for clinical expectations at each stage of the program. Provide instruction in core nurse anesthesia course content, with emphasis on clinical practicum courses. Advise learners on clinical progression and professional development. Serve as faculty advisor for learner DNP scholarly projects, especially quality improvement projects based at clinical sites. Collect and report clinical outcome data for program evaluation and the COA annual report. Participate in preparation for the COA accreditation site visit. Serve on the Admissions Committee for review and selection of candidates for admission. Serve on the Curriculum Committee and contribute to curriculum assessment and revision to meet COA and CCNE curriculum and learner outcome standards. Qualifications Required Qualifications Doctoral degree (PhD, EdD, or DNP) from an institution of higher education accredited by an agency recognized by the US Secretary of Education at the time the degree was conferred. Current unencumbered license, or eligibility for licensure, as a registered nurse and advanced practice registered nurse (APRN) in North Carolina. Current certification or recertification as a Certified Registered Nurse Anesthetist (CRNA) from the National Board of Certification and Recertification for Nurse Anesthetists (NBCRNA). Current Advanced Cardiac Life Support (ACLS) and Pediatric Advanced Life Support (PALS) certifications. Minimum of three years of clinical experience as a CRNA. Formal education in curriculum, instruction, and evaluation. Experience as a clinical preceptor, clinical instructor, or clinical coordinator for nurse anesthesia learners. Preferred Qualifications Experience developing clinical sites or managing clinical affiliation agreements. Experience with clinical case tracking systems. Teaching and academic administrative experience. Certified Nurse Educator (CNE) credential. Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/166221": {
      "title": "Academic Fieldwork Coordinator and Faculty, Occupational Therapy Program",
      "description": "Academic Fieldwork Coordinator and Faculty, Occupational Therapy Program You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Academic Fieldwork Coordinator and Faculty, Occupational Therapy Program Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Faculty Apply Description Academic Fieldwork Coordinator (AFWC) Doctor of Occupational Therapy Program Assistant or Associate Professor, Tenure Track The Department of Occupational Therapy at Methodist University in Fayetteville, North Carolina, is seeking an Academic Fieldwork Coordinator to lead clinical education in our in-person, entry-level Doctor of Occupational Therapy (OTD) program, which admits cohorts of 30 students. This is an opportunity to shape a growing fieldwork program and build lasting partnerships across a region with diverse practice settings, including military and veteran health services connected to Fort Bragg, the Cape Fear Valley Health system, rural and community-based practice. You will join a collaborative, student-centered faculty at a university that also includes a School of Medicine and an expanding set of graduate health professions programs. What you'll do Lead the development, implementation, and evaluation of Level I and Level II fieldwork in alignment with the curriculum design and ACOTE standards Build and maintain a strong network of fieldwork sites, including affiliation agreements, site development, and responsive, professional communication with clinical partners Train and support fieldwork educators Conduct site visits, either virtually or in person Manage student placements, fieldwork records, and student compliance requirements (such as immunizations and background checks) using Exxat Prepare, advise, and support students before and during fieldwork, including managing remediation and performance concerns Serve as instructor of record for fieldwork courses Coordinate with the Doctoral Capstone Coordinator to keep fieldwork and capstone experiences aligned Use fieldwork outcomes data to inform program evaluation, and contribute to accreditation reports and self-studies Teach in your area of expertise and contribute to advising, scholarship, and service. The position includes dedicated administrative time for fieldwork coordination and a clinical practice day each week, so you can maintain your clinical skills while you teach. Scholarship in fieldwork and clinical education is supported and valued for tenure and promotion. Appointment This is a 12-month, full-time, on-campus, tenure-track faculty position in an in-person program. Rank and salary are commensurate with experience. To apply Priority review of applications begins October 26, 2026, and continues until the position is filled. The anticipated start date is as soon as possible. Apply through Methodist University's employment portal. Please submit: Letter of application Curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy Contact information for three references For questions about the position, contact Dr. Katie Jones, EdD, OTR/L, Chair, Department of Occupational Therapy, and OTD Program Director, at kjones@methodist.edu or (910) 630-7216. Qualifications Required qualifications Doctoral degree (OTD, PhD, EdD, DSc, or related) from an accredited institution Licensed as an occupational therapist in North Carolina, or eligible for licensure with an active NC license by the start date At least 2 years of clinical practice experience as an occupational therapist Experience as a fieldwork educator, or documented training in fieldwork educator roles and responsibilities (for example, the AOTA Fieldwork Educator Certificate Program) Preferred qualifications Experience in academic fieldwork coordination Experience with ACOTE accreditation processes Experience with Exxat or a similar clinical education platform Teaching experience in higher education Expertise in mental health, assistive technology, or program development An established area of clinical expertise and interest in scholarship related to fieldwork education Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/165561": {
      "title": "Doctoral Capstone Coordinator and Faculty, Occupational Therapy",
      "description": "Doctoral Capstone Coordinator and Faculty, Occupational Therapy You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Doctoral Capstone Coordinator and Faculty, Occupational Therapy Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Faculty Apply Description Job Title: Doctoral Capstone Coordinator and Faculty, Occupational Therapy Department: Occupational Therapy Program: Doctor of Occupational Therapy (OTD) College/Division: College of Health Sciences and Human Services Location: Fayetteville, NC Appointment: 12-month, tenure-track faculty. Rank commensurate with academic experience. Position Summary Methodist University invites applications for a Doctoral Capstone Coordinator to join the Doctor of Occupational Therapy (OTD) program. This is a full-time, 12-month, tenure-track faculty position. The Doctoral Capstone Coordinator serves as the primary faculty member responsible for the development, implementation, coordination, and evaluation of the doctoral capstone component of the OTD curriculum in accordance with the Accreditation Council for Occupational Therapy Education (ACOTE) standards. Grounded in Methodist University's commitment to scholarship, service, and the development of the whole person, the Doctoral Capstone Coordinator fosters an educational environment that supports students in producing capstone work of doctoral-level rigor and professional relevance. The coordinator serves as a liaison among students, capstone sites, and capstone mentors, and is responsible for cultivating and maintaining collaborative partnerships that support the capstone experience and project. In addition to capstone coordination, the position carries a reduced teaching load in the OTD curriculum. Position Responsibilities Capstone Coordination Oversee all aspects of the doctoral capstone process, ensuring program compliance with ACOTE Section D.1.0 standards. This includes, but is not limited to: Identifying, developing, and maintaining capstone sites and corresponding affiliation agreements. Collaborating with students, faculty, and content mentors to design individualized capstone experiences and projects, including specific objectives, supervision plans, mentorship structures, and evaluation mechanisms, aligned with program mission and curriculum design. Collaborating with the Academic Fieldwork Coordinator to ensure consistent communication of program needs with sites that provide both fieldwork and doctoral capstone experience placements. Ensuring preparation for doctoral capstone experiences includes literature reviews, needs assessments, goals and objectives, and outcome evaluation plans prior to commencement. Monitoring student progress and evaluating student performance and ability to integrate didactic knowledge, evidence, theory, and professional reasoning into the capstone experience and project. Providing orientation, training, and ongoing support to capstone site supervisors and content mentors. Maintaining organized documentation of all capstone-related records, including affiliation agreements, compliance materials, student logs, mentor credentials, and evaluation data. Facilitating the completion and dissemination of individual doctoral capstone projects. Instructional Responsibilities Teach capstone-related coursework and additional courses within area of expertise as determined in coordination with the Program Director. Facilitate student learning in alignment with course and program learning outcomes. Contribute to ongoing curriculum development, assessment, and continuous improvement activities. Provide timely feedback, academic advising, and mentorship to students. Maintain regular office hours. Scholarship Engage in scholarly activities consistent with tenure-track expectations and the OTD program's strategic goals. Contribute to the profession through peer-reviewed publications, presentations, grant activity, or other forms of scholarship as agreed upon with the Program Director. Service Participate in department, college, and university committees and governance activities. Contribute to admissions, recruitment, and programmatic planning efforts. Engage in professional organizations and community service consistent with the mission of Methodist University and the OTD program. Application Instructions Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy, and the names and contact information of three professional references. About Methodist University Methodist University is a private institution located in Fayetteville, North Carolina, committed to developing the whole person through scholarship, service, and ethical leadership. The university serves a diverse student community and values innovation, academic excellence, and engagement with the broader community. Qualifications Required Qualifications Doctoral degree (OTD, PhD, EdD, or other terminal degree) awarded by an institution that is accredited by a USDE-recognized institutional accrediting agency. Candidates who are near completion of a doctoral program will be considered. Occupational therapy degree from an ACOTE-accredited program. Certification by NBCOT as a Registered Occupational Therapist (OTR). Licensed as an occupational therapist in North Carolina, or eligible for licensure prior to start date. Minimum of two years of clinical practice as an occupational therapist, with at least one year of formal teaching experience (adjunct or full-time) at the postsecondary level. Knowledge of ACOTE standards, particularly those related to doctoral capstone education. Preferred Qualifications Expertise in the research process or community program development. Priority consideration will be given to candidates with demonstrated experience in one or both of these areas. Experience coordinating or directing capstone, fieldwork, or experiential learning programs in an ACOTE-accredited program. Record of peer-reviewed scholarly activity. Experience with online learning management systems. Active involvement in professional occupational therapy organizations. Demonstrated ability to develop and sustain community and clinical partnerships. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Thorough understanding of ACOTE accreditation requirements related to doctoral capstone education. Effective organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work collaboratively across disciplines and with external partners. Demonstrated commitment to fostering academic integrity and student-centered learning. Proficiency with learning management systems and standard office technology. Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/165324": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor - Legal Studies",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor - Legal Studies You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Instructor - Legal Studies Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Adjunct Faculty Apply Description Description The Division of Social Sciences at Methodist University is looking for adjunct faculty in the Legal Studies. We offer a variety of courses in the various forms of the legal system and are specifically looking for faculty who can teach the following courses: Introduction to Law, Environmental Regulations, Legal Research and Writing, Law and the Legal System, Tort Law, Contract Law, among others. Part-time adjunct instructors can teach up to three courses per semester and will be responsible for developing and delivering course content (in line with course and programmatic outcomes), grading assignments, and providing feedback to students. If you are interested in this opportunity, please apply through our website and include your CV and cover letter.  For questions about the position, please contact Dr. Chris Cronin, Division Head of Social Sciences, ccronin@methodist.edu Review of applications will begin immediately and will be considered on a rolling basis as teaching needs arise. Qualifications Education: A minimum of a JD and some teaching experience, or experienced professionals (5 years or more) in the field. Experience: Preferably at least one year of classroom teaching experience and/or online teaching experience. Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/165219": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor - Criminal Justice and Military Science",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor - Criminal Justice and Military Science You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Instructor - Criminal Justice and Military Science Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Adjunct Faculty Apply Description Description The Division of Criminal Justice and Military Science at Methodist University is looking for adjunct faculty to teach JUS 3100 Law and the Legal System and JUS 3890 Criminal Evidence and Procedure, among others. Part-time adjunct instructors will be responsible for developing and delivering course content (in line with course and programmatic outcomes), grading assignments, and providing feedback to students. If you are interested in this opportunity, please apply through our website and include your CV and cover letter.  For questions about the position, please contact Dr. Bryan Brendley, Division Head of Criminal Justice and Military Science, bbrendley@methodist.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue on a rolling basis as teaching needs arise. Qualified candidates are invited to submit a CV and letter of interest. Qualifications Education: A minimum of a JD and some teaching experience, or experienced professionals (5 years or more) in the field. Experience: Preferably at least one year of classroom teaching experience and/or online teaching experience. Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/165084": {
      "title": "Academic and Career Advisor",
      "description": "Academic and Career Advisor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Academic and Career Advisor Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description The Academic and Career Advisor supports the mission, goals and objectives of Methodist University.  The Academic and Career Advisor reports to the Associate Director for One Stop Academic Services and is a member of the One Stop team . Core Duties and Responsibilities: Serve a caseload of up to 300 students, offering holistic assessment, individualized planning support, and proactive academic and career advising. Work with each new student in their first year at MU to develop an Individual Academic Plan, which includes a clear Degree Pathway, an Individual Career Development plan, and a faculty mentor assignment. Support and guide students, with sound equity and inclusion practices, as they explore their personal, academic, and professional interests, acquire career readiness competencies, and achieve their academic goals. Collaborate closely with faculty in academic programs to stay up to date on curricular changes and to provide insight into potential barriers to student success. Assist students with finding work-based professional learning experiences and career exploration opportunities. Evaluate student needs and provide appropriate resource referral to career, academic, counseling, and student life resources and opportunities. Collaborate with faculty, coaches, staff, and other One Stop staff for student intervention and advocacy. Recommend actions related to academic alert, probation, suspension, and dismissal of students. Utilize advising and student success technologies for outreach to students. Engage ongoing professional development and training to maintain knowledge about advising concepts. Perform other duties related to student success as assigned. Qualifications Education, Experience, and Essential Skills Master’s degree preferred in advising or higher education related discipline Experience in advising/career coaching for students in university settings. Strong commitment to equity, inclusion, and to working with diverse student populations. Strong understanding of student development theory and high-impact practices in retention and graduation initiatives. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills Ability to adapt advising/coaching style to meet the needs of each student Proficiency with online tools, resources, and advising methods and a commitment to continuously improving services to students Ability to prioritize multiple responsibilities and work independently Ability to communicate effectively at all levels of the institution Well-developed sense of professional ethics. Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/164995": {
      "title": "Director of Annual Giving and Digital Engagement",
      "description": "Director of Annual Giving and Digital Engagement You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Director of Annual Giving and Digital Engagement Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description JOB SUMMARY Reporting to the Vice President for Institutional Advancement, the Director of Annual Giving and Digital Engagement provides strategic leadership for Methodist University’s comprehensive annual giving program while integrating digital engagement strategies to expand donor participation, retention, and philanthropic growth. This position oversees the planning, execution, and continuous improvement of all annual fund initiatives, including direct mail, faculty and staff giving, senior class gifts, year-end appeals, and leadership annual giving efforts, while incorporating data-driven digital marketing strategies, segmentation, automation, and analytics to enhance donor experience and performance outcomes. The Director plays a central role in building a culture of philanthropy that advances student success and strengthens the University’s long-term donor pipeline. Works closely with departmental staff for all activities involving the Founders Council, including its annual golf and tennis events. Duties include volunteer and event coordination, publicity, and mailings. In coordination with the Vice President for Institutional Advancement is responsible for all other Annual Fund appeals, including direct mail and annual appeals, and other campaigns. The director is responsible for identifying and engaging volunteer and donor prospects, writing appeal letters, and analyzing campaign results to increase annual funding for the University. Visits, calls , and cultivates existing and prospective donor portfolio as assigned by the Vice President for Institutional Advancement Assists with all other Advancement duties as assigned. CORE RESPONSIBILITIES Strategic Annual Giving Leadership Develop and implement a comprehensive, multi-channel annual giving strategy aligned with institutional priorities. Manage all annual fund solicitations, including direct mail, digital campaigns, senior class gifts, faculty/staff giving, and annual appeals. Identify opportunities to expand and innovate the annual giving program through digital tools, and emerging best practices. Analyze campaign performance and give trends to inform strategy and improve participation and revenue outcomes. Digital Engagement & Marketing Integration Lead digital fundraising efforts including email campaigns, online giving initiatives, social media fundraising, and targeted digital appeals. Utilize audience segmentation, automation, and analytics to personalize donor communications and optimize donor journeys. Collaborate closely with Marketing & Communications to ensure cohesive messaging, brand alignment, and integrated campaign execution. Monitor digital engagement metrics and conversion rates to increase online giving and donor retention. Donor Cultivation & Portfolio Management Maintain a portfolio of primary annual giving and leadership-level prospects. Develop identification, cultivation and solicitation strategies that move donors toward increased engagement and giving levels. Make solicitations and steward donors in a timely and strategic manner. Maintain accurate and timely reporting in the Raiser’s Edge system. Founders Council & Volunteer Leadership Serve as University liaison and advisor to the Founders Council. Oversee recruitment, solicitation, orientation, and engagement of Council members. Coordinate Founders Council board meetings and strategic initiatives. Lead collaboration with staff and volunteers for the annual golf and tennis events. Identify and recruit prospective volunteer leaders to support annual giving growth. Events & Engagement Programming Assist in coordinating alumni and annual fund-related events, including Homecoming, regional gatherings, reunions, scholarship luncheons, and recognition dinners. Support volunteer coordination and donor engagement activities both on and off campus. Host on-campus donor visits and assist with stewardship experiences that deepen long-term philanthropic relationships. Community Representation Represent the University at community and civic events, including Chamber of Commerce activities, symposiums, receptions, and other outreach opportunities. Advancement Office Collaboration Assist with Advancement initiatives, including the Annual Report, Endowed Scholarship Luncheon, Homecoming, President’s Society Reception and other donor recognition events. Participate in departmental planning, goal setting, and budget preparation. Contribute to short- and long-term advancement strategy development, including campaign readiness and pipeline growth. Project management and organizational leadership. Qualifications The candidate must: Possess a bachelor’s degree (required). Masters degree preferred. Have three to five years of experience in annual fund, alumni relations, digital fundraising, or similar constituent outreach programs. Demonstrate strong written and verbal communication skills. Show evidence of leadership, planning, and organizational ability. Be proficient in Microsoft Office applications. Be familiar with constituent management databases; Raiser’s Edge experience preferred. Have knowledge of working with volunteers and volunteer boards. Demonstrate strong understanding of digital engagement tools, segmentation, and analytics. Exhibit imagination, integrity, and the ability to work effectively in a team-oriented environment. Be highly self-motivated and able to follow Advancement Office policies and procedures. Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/164901": {
      "title": "Grounds Maintenance Technician",
      "description": "Grounds Maintenance Technician You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Grounds Maintenance Technician Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description This position reports to the Superintendent of Grounds. Duties include, but are not limited to: Planting, weeding, mulching, watering, and caring for plants and shrubbery on university grounds. Mowing Maintaining lawns, trees, shrubs, flowers, turf, and irrigation. Trimming hedges, trees, and shrubs. Preventing and eliminating weeds. Maintaining university grounds by keeping them free from trash, litter, and debris.  Tent setups. Lifting/moving objects and equipment weighing approximately 50 pounds as needed. Using hand and power tools as needed to accomplish assigned tasks. Frequent bending, kneeling, lifting, and shoveling. Must be able to work weekends as needed. Qualifications Experience and Training: Any combination of experience and training that would likely provide the required knowledge and abilities is qualifying. Prefer applicants with strong grounds or horticultural experience. Prefer applicants with education equivalent to the completion of the twelfth grade. Valid Driver's License required. Knowledge of: Proper weeding, trimming, pruning, and fertilizing of plants and shrubbery. Hazards and safety precautions related to general maintenance and horticultural activities. Ability to: Properly care for assigned areas and equipment. Understand and carry out oral and written directions. Establish and maintain effective working relationships with those contacted in the course of work. Communicate effectively, both orally and in writing. Work outdoors in all weather conditions. Bend, kneel, lift, and shovel. Lift/move heavy equipment and objects as needed. Properly use and care for hand and power tools. Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/164424": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor Criminal Justice",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor Criminal Justice You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Instructor Criminal Justice Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Adjunct Faculty Apply Description Description The Division of Criminal Justice and Military Science at Methodist University is looking for adjunct faculty for the Criminal Justice Program for the 2026-2027 academic year. We offer a variety of courses in the various forms of the criminal justice system, and are specifically looking for faculty who can teach in the areas of corrections, policing, victimology, etc. Part-time instructors can teach up to three courses per semester and will be responsible for developing and delivering course content (in line with course and programmatic outcomes), grading assignments, and providing feedback to students. If you are interested in this opportunity, please apply through our website and include your CV and cover letter.  For questions about the position, please contact Dr. Bryan Brendley, Division Head of Criminal Justice and Military Science, bbrendley@methodist.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the positions are filled. Qualified candidates are invited to submit a CV and letter of interest. Qualifications Education: A minimum of an MA in Criminal Justice, Criminology or Justice Studies and some teaching experience, or experienced professionals (5 years or more) in the field. Experience: Preferably at least one year of classroom teaching experience and/or online teaching experience. Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/164309": {
      "title": "Security Sergeant",
      "description": "Security Sergeant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Security Sergeant Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Salary Range $15.00 Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Job Description Reports to: Captain of Security, Assistant Director of Public Safety Job Details: Full time, 40 hours a week, Hourly General Description Security Shift Supervisors support the mission, goals, and objectives of the University, and that of the Department of Public Safety. Specific duties and responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Protecting the Methodist University Community (Students, Faculty, Staff and Guests) from theft, vandalism, and any disruption of the educational process Covering shift when others are out or on leave Securing campus facilities either by your presence or through the building security plan Following in detail the Public Safety Manual of procedures and any directives of the Director or any supervisory staff within the Public Safety Department Accounting for, inspecting, briefing and supervising personnel assigned to your shift Conducting on-the-job training as necessary Assisting subordinates in resolving problems that affect their duty performance such as obtaining clothing and equipment needed. Ensuring personnel problems such as pay discrepancies are brought to the Chain of Command’s attention in a timely manner and following up to see that employees work-related problems are corrected. Counseling employees on their job performance Exercising direct command in a way that assures the good order, conduct, discipline and efficiency of subordinates. Completing and filing of all forms, such as: 1. Incident Reports 2. Daily Reports 3. Maintenance Reports 4. Safety Reports 5. Other Reports as Required In addition, you are responsible to fulfill all rules, regulations, and guidelines of Methodist University, and to always be a proper role model for the students and your subordinates. Finally, you are responsible for fulfilling other duties as assigned by the Director of Public Safety, and any other senior supervisor assigned to the Public Safety Department. Job Qualifications Education Requirements: High School Other Requirements: Security/Law Enforcement experience Supervisory experience Field training officer experience preferred Pass a comprehensive background check Pass an oral interview Possess a valid driver’s license Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/164130": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Advanced Paramedicine",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor of Advanced Paramedicine You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Instructor of Advanced Paramedicine Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Adjunct Faculty Apply Description The Advanced Paramedicine Program at Methodist University is seeking adjunct faculty to teach courses in its Bachelor of Science in Advanced Paramedicine program. Embedded within the College of Health Sciences and Human Services, the Advanced Paramedicine program prepares experienced paramedics to expand their clinical knowledge and professional practice and to pursue opportunities in advanced clinical practice, education, leadership, research, and other healthcare professions. Adjunct instructors are responsible for teaching online courses in curricular areas related to advanced patient assessment and clinical reasoning, pathophysiology and physiology, pharmacology, advanced airway and ventilator management, trauma and critical care, maternal/fetal and pediatric medicine, advanced diagnostics and electrocardiography, toxicology, research, leadership, and other areas relevant to advanced paramedicine practice. Interested persons should submit a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy statement (no more than 1-page in length), and a statement that articulates their approach to teaching or other initiatives designed to foster a sense of student engagement, community, and belonging (not to exceed 1-page in length).  The letter of interest should identify the area(s) of the curriculum you are interested in teaching in along with an explanation of your qualifications to teach courses in that area(s). Qualifications Master's degree or higher in Paramedicine, Emergency Medical Services, Health Sciences, Education, or a related field Professional experience and expertise relevant to the course(s) to be taught Experience teaching at the undergraduate or graduate level preferred Experience teaching online and familiarity with Canvas Learning Management System preferred Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/164101": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Healthcare Administration",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor of Healthcare Administration You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Instructor of Healthcare Administration Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Part Time Apply Description The Healthcare Administration program at Methodist University is seeking adjunct faculty to teach courses at the bachelor’s level. Embedded within the College of Health Sciences and Human Services, the Healthcare Administration program prepares students for management and leadership careers across the health sector. Adjunct instructors are responsible for teaching online courses in curricular areas related to medical terminology, healthcare leadership, quality assessment and performance improvement, organizational behavior, economics and finance of healthcare organizations, disaster management, global health, conflict resolution, health insurance and managed care, cultural competence in healthcare and research methods. Interested persons should submit a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy statement (no more than 1-page in length), and a statement that articulates their approach to teaching or other initiatives designed to foster a sense of student engagement, community, and belonging (not to exceed 1-page in length).  The letter of interest should identify the area(s) of the curriculum you are interested in teaching in along with an explanation of your qualifications to teach courses in that area(s). Qualifications Qualifications Master's degree or higher in Healthcare Administration or a related field; doctoral degree preferred Professional experience and expertise relevant to the course(s) to be taught Experience teaching at the undergraduate or graduate level preferred Experience teaching online and familiarity with Canvas Learning Management System preferred Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/163838": {
      "title": "Chair & Head, School of Nursing",
      "description": "Chair & Head, School of Nursing You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Chair & Head, School of Nursing Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Faculty Apply Description Position Title: Chair & Head of Nursing; Full‑Time Tenure‑Track Faculty (Assistant or Associate Professor) Department / School: School of Nursing, College of Health Sciences & Human Services, Methodist University Position Reports To: Dean, College of Health Sciences & Human Services Position Anticipated Start Date: August 1, 2027 Position Summary As the Head of the School of Nursing, you will lead Methodist University’s growing nursing programs, including Pre‑licensure BSN, RN‑to‑BSN, DNP, and any future degrees. You oversee curriculum, accreditation and compliance, faculty development, student success, clinical partnerships, scholarship, and participation in institutional governance—ensuring full alignment with NC Board of Nursing requirements and CCNE accreditation standards. Essential Functions & Responsibilities Leadership & Academic Governance Provide vision and leadership in developing all nursing program offerings in accordance with regulatory and accreditation bodies. Recruit, supervise and mentor nursing faculty, staff and clinical instructors; foster professional development. Lead faculty governance, strategic planning, budgeting, and school-level initiatives. Collaborate with fellow program directors and chairs within the College of Health Sciences and Human Services (CHSHS) to promote and implement interprofessional educational opportunities. Curriculum, Accreditation & Regulatory Compliance Direct ongoing curriculum evaluation, mapping, and revision to align with professional and regulatory standards. Monitor key program outcomes (NCLEX pass rates, retention, remediation, graduate outcomes) and submit required reports to regulatory agencies. Coordinate CCNE self-studies, annual reports, and site visits. Administrative & Resource Management Oversee program budget, develop funding proposals, and support simulation resource acquisition. Collaborate with institutional advancement to secure grants or support aligned with strategic goals. Clinical Partnerships & Practice Coordination Oversee and maintain clinical affiliation agreements, including for Dedicated Education Units (DEUs) with partner systems. Ensure clinical hours, preceptor assignments, and simulation Teaching & Student Advising Support orientation and transition programs for first‑degree and RN‑to‑BSN students. Advise students on progression, academic planning, and professional development. Teach in area(s) of clinical expertise within nursing curriculum (didactic, simulation, and clinical) courses. Scholarship, Professional Engagement & Service Maintain an active record of scholarship (peer-reviewed publications, presentations, or innovations) in nursing education. Represent the program in professional nursing and academic organizations, foster community and clinical partnerships. Serve on university-level committees, advising boards, accreditation task forces, and regional health education initiatives. Working Conditions Full-time faculty workload with responsibilities in teaching, administration, scholarship, and service. Supervisory responsibility for full-time faculty, clinical instructors, and support staff. Availability for occasional evening/weekend commitments tied to accreditation visits, clinical site oversight, or department events. Application Instructions Submit materials—including CV, cover letter addressing leadership experience, statement of teaching philosophy, and contact information for three references—via Methodist University's online application portal. Qualifications Required Earned doctoral degree (e.g., DNP, PhD) in Nursing or related discipline. Current, unencumbered RN licensure in North Carolina and eligibility for NC BON program leadership oversight. Minimum of 5 years’ experience in nursing education leadership (e.g., curriculum development, accreditation management, and/or chair/director role). Evidence of collaborative leadership and teaching excellence. Preferred Experience with CCNE-accredited undergraduate nursing programs. Demonstrated scholarly work in nursing education, leadership, or clinical practice. Established partnerships with clinical agencies in southeast North Carolina. Certification as nurse educator (CNE) or healthcare simulation educator (CHSE) preferred. Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/163748": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of History",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor of History You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Instructor of History Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Adjunct Faculty Apply Description Job Location: Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC Position Type: Adjunct Faculty Description The History Department in the Division of Humanities at Methodist University is looking for an adjunct instructor to teach an in-person course in an engaging and rigorous manner.  The instructor must be able to teach World History I or United States History I in Spring 2026 on campus either MWF or Tuesday-Thursday.  A successful candidate will be considered for future courses. Responsibilities: Teach one section of World History I (to 1500) or United States History I (to 1865) during the Fall 2026 semester. Provide quality in-person instruction, including the delivery of constructive feedback and evaluation on student work in a timely manner. Communicate with students to support them and address their questions or concerns. Required Materials: Cover letter, CV, and transcripts (unofficial copies are acceptable for initial application). The review of applicants will begin immediately, and applications will also be accepted and reviewed for future adjunct opportunities beyond the Spring 2026 semester. For questions about the position, please contact Dr. Patrick W. O’Neil, Program Coordinator of History and Division Head of Humanities: poneil@methodist.edu Qualifications Minimum Requirements: A Master’s degree in History is required, with at least 18 credit hours at the graduate level, from an accredited institution. Teaching Experience preferred, with a record of student engagement. Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/162995": {
      "title": "Facilities Maintenance Plumber",
      "description": "Facilities Maintenance Plumber You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Facilities Maintenance Plumber Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description Purpose of Position The Facilities Maintenance Plumber serves as an essential member of the Methodist University Facilities Maintenance team and is responsible for maintaining safe, dependable, and efficient plumbing systems throughout campus . This position supports the university community by ensuring facilities remain ope r ational, well-maintained, and prepared to support students, faculty , staff, and guests . The role requires more than completing repairs. A Facilities Maintenance Plumber is expected to take ownership of assigned areas, identify concerns before they become failures , protect university resources, and contribute to a department culture built on pride, professionalism, teamwork, and continuous improvement. Department Philosophy The Facilities Maintenance Department believes that the condition of our campus is a reflection of our commitment to those we serve. Our team strives to provide a clean, safe , reliable , and welcoming environment by maintaining a high standard of excellence in every task performed. Key Responsibilities Plumbing Systems Maintenance Maintain , troubleshoot , repair, and install campus plumbing systems including : Domestic hot and cold water systems San i tary sewer and storm drainage systems Natural gas piping Pumps and circulation systems Valves , regulators , and controls Water heaters and storage tanks Commercial kitchen plumbing systems Laboratory plumbing equipment Mechanical room piping systems Repair and replace faucets and fixtures , toilets and urinals, flush valves, mi x ing valves , drinking fountains and bottle fillers , shower systems , drain components , piping , and fittings. Maintain , troubleshoot , repair , and install tankless water heating systems , including associated controls , venting, recirculation systems, and manufacturer-recommended preventative maintenance. Participate in the department's rotating after-hours emergency call schedule and respond to plumbing and facility emergencies as required. Preventative Maintenance Expectations The Facilities Maintenance Plumber is e x pected to support a proactive ma i ntenance approach by : Performing scheduled inspections of plumbing systems and equipment. Identifying potential issues before equipment failure occurs . Documenting deficiencies and corrective actions . Maintaining accurate equipment history and records . Recommending improvements that increase reliability and efficiency . Supporting development and improvement of department SOPs. Facilities Team Expectations Every member of Facilities Maintenance is expected to: Take ownership of the campus and treat facilities as if they were their own. Perform repairs correctly , not just temporarily. Maintain clean and organized work areas . Communicate professionally with students , faculty , staff , and coworkers . Assist other trades when needed . Look beyond the original request and identify additional issues . Represent the department with professionalism and pride . Participate in the department's rotating on-call schedule and respond to emergency maintenance situations outside normal working hours as required. Cross-Departmental Support The Facilities Maintenance Plumber is expected to work collaboratively with all Facilities Maintenance personnel to accomplish departmental goals and support the University's mission. While plumbing is the employee's primary area of responsibility, this position will : Assist HVAC, electrical, carpentry, painting, locksmith, grounds, and general maintenance personnel with projects and repairs as workload and operational needs require. Support campus events, special projects, emergency response, and weather-related operations. Share knowledge and assist coworkers in resolving maintenance issues while promoting teamwork and continuous improvement. Maintain flexibility in daily assignments to meet changing departmental priorities and provide the highest level of service to the University community. Contribute to a positive team environment by demonstrating professionalism, cooperation, and a willingness to assist wherever needed. Safety Responsibilities The Facilities Maintenance Plumber will : Follow OSHA standards and university safety policies. Practice proper lockout/tagout procedures. Maintain safe job sites . Use tools and equipment correctly . Report unsafe conditions immediately . Ensure repairs meet applicable plumbing codes and standards . Qualifications Required Skills and Experience High school diploma or equivalent. 3-5 years of plumbing , maintenance , or related trade experience preferred . Strong troubleshooting and repair skills . Knowledge of commercial plumbing systems . Ability to work independently with minimal supervision. Ability to prioritize emergency and routine work. Basic computer proficiency , including Microsoft Outlook , Microsoft Word , Microsoft Excel , and computerized maintenance/work order (CMMS) systems. Valid driver ' s license. Preferred Qualifications Plumbing license or certification. Backflow prevention certification. Experience maintaining and troubleshooting commercial tankless water heating systems. Institutional or campus maintenance experience. Knowledge of preventative maintenance programs . Professional Standard A Methodist University Facilities Maintenance employee understands that every repair, inspection, interaction, and project contributes to the overall campus experience. Our goal is not simply to fix problems - our goal is to build trust , create solutions , protect university assets , and leave every space better than we found it. Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/162627": {
      "title": "Biostatistician, School of Medicine",
      "description": "Biostatistician, School of Medicine You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Biostatistician, School of Medicine School of Medicine Location - Fayetteville, NC 28304 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Faculty Apply Description Methodist University Cape Fear Valley Health School of Medicine, located in the vibrant and diverse community of Fayetteville, NC, is poised for growth and innovation as a candidate school with the LCME, with a start date of summer 2026 for its charter class currently enrolled. Our mission is bold yet vital: to prepare the next generation of socially accountable, equity-focused, community-engaged physician leaders committed to reducing health disparities and improving outcomes in southeastern North Carolina and beyond. We are looking for a proactive, resourceful, self-directed, and highly organized biostatistician with experience in data science and/or epidemiological methods. The statistician will report to the Associate Dean of Research and is expected to work with both faculty and students on the design, analysis, and dissemination of research projects. In addition, the statistician will contribute to teaching as well as supporting our office of student assessment. Qualified candidates are invited to submit: • A letter of application; • Curriculum vitae; • Evidence of teaching effectiveness and a sample publication • A concise equity and diversity statement about research, teaching, or other experiences, successes, and challenges in working with diverse investigators and student; and • Contact information for three references. General responsibilities: As the biostatistician you will support biomedical research projects across the medical school and contribute to teaching. Your responsibilities include: Collaborating with faculty to design and conduct research projects. Mentoring students and provide technical guidance on study design, data analysis, and manuscript preparation. Contributing to dissemination of research findings including conference abstracts, presentations, and manuscripts for publication. Contributing to developing grant proposals. Teaching research and biostatistical concepts in the medical curriculum. Supporting the Office of Assessment in data analytics, visualization, and reporting related to student learning, curriculum evaluation, and institutional effectiveness. Other duties as assigned You will be expected to work with large existing datasets such as Epic Cosmos, NHANES, and NIS, and be familiar with longitudinal data analyses as well as machine learning. With the focus of the school on improving health and health access to our community, you will be expected to work with community partners and contribute to epidemiological studies. May require attendance at meetings outside \"regular duty hours\" Qualifications Education/Work experience Minimal qualifications Master’s degree in (bio)statistics or related field and 2 years relevant experience. Demonstrated contributions to significant projects or additional doctoral education may substitute for experience. Proven proficiency in at least one statistical programming language, such as SAS or R. Experience processing and analyzing large, multi-source datasets, with the ability to execute statistical analyses, develop analytical reports, and maintain high-quality documentation on time. Excellent oral and written communication skills Preferred qualifications Knowledge of data modeling and additional specialized software (e.g. SQL, Python). Broad understanding of medical physiology, anatomy, and processes to be able to give consultative services across various medical disciplines. Contributing to clinical research projects, manuscript preparation or other written summaries of results. Collaborating with professionals who have various levels of statistical understanding. Teaching and mentoring professional/graduate level students. Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/162136": {
      "title": "Program Director for MS in Clinical Mental Health Counseling, Open Rank",
      "description": "Program Director for MS in Clinical Mental Health Counseling, Open Rank You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Program Director for MS in Clinical Mental Health Counseling, Open Rank Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Apply Description Job Summary Methodist University invites applications for a Director of the Master in Science Program in Clinical Mental Health Counseling (CMHC), housed in the Division of Social Sciences. Salary for this non tenure-track, 12-month position is commensurate with professional and academic experience. This is a non-remote appointment; presence on the Methodist University campus in Fayetteville, North Carolina is required. Job Responsibilities include: Planning, implementation, and oversight of the CMHC academic program Oversee the recruitment, hiring, and development of qualified faculty and staff to meet the goals of the program Establish and maintain relationships locally, regionally, and nationally to support clinical sites/clinical affiliations Oversee the program’s initial and ongoing CACREP accreditation process Teach core graduate-level coursework in a hybrid format Employ best practices in assessment of student learning and academic program outcomes Contribute scholarly and professional development efforts in the mental health discipline. Maintain and organize regulatory and compliance documents, reports, and other metrics using electronic media Engage in service to the Clinical Mental Health program, the College of Health Sciences and Human Services, and the university Perform other related duties as assigned for the success of the program and division Applications: Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For full consideration , qualified applicants are invited to submit the following: 1) letter of intent, 2) curriculum vitae, 3) teaching philosophy statement, 4) transcripts, and 5) concise statement about your approach to teaching or other initiatives designed to foster a sense of student engagement, community, and belonging. For inquiries, contact Dr. Jeffry Thigpen, Head for the Division of Human Services ( jthigpen@methodist.edu ). All applications should be submitted through http://www.methodist.edu/positions-available . Qualifications Experience, Education & Other Qualifications: Doctoral degree in Mental Health Counseling Minimum of three years of clinical experience Professional identity in the Counseling Profession Minimum of three years of higher education experience with successful teaching Licensed in North Carolina as a Licensed Clinical Mental Health Counselor or eligible to seek and gain licensure Experience with the CACREP accreditation process Experience teaching in a fully online degree program Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/162051": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Clinical Mental Health Counseling/Clinical Placement Coordinator",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Clinical Mental Health Counseling/Clinical Placement Coordinator You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Professor in Clinical Mental Health Counseling/Clinical Placement Coordinator Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Faculty Apply Description The Department of Clinical Mental Health Counseling at Methodist University invites applications for a 12-month, non-tenure-track Assistant Professor position beginning August 2026. The Master of Science program in Clinical Mental Health Counseling is online and embedded in the Division of Human Services in the College of Health Sciences and Human Services. The Department of Clinical Mental Health Counseling is seeking an experienced Clinical Placement Coordinator to provide leadership related to practicum and internship placement, skill development, and supervision.  This is a non-remote appointment; presence on the Methodist University campus in Fayetteville, North Carolina is required. Essential Job Functions: Teach core graduate-level coursework in a hybrid format Employ best practices in assessment of student learning and academic program outcomes Develop, plan, and execute strategies to coordinate students’ internship/practicum and field experience opportunities across the United States Serve as liaison with students, other educators, staff, and outside community agencies and partners in facilitating program objectives, including but not limited to developing, and facilitating residency workshops, coordinating logistics, site vetting, site supervision, training and other student activities and duties Create and maintain partnerships with mental health organizations Participate in accreditation and program approval standards for clinical mental health counseling, especially as they relate to field experiences and supervision at sites and at the university Engage and collaborate with other educators and staff to identify and solve problems and improve the program Contribute scholarly and professional development efforts in the mental health discipline. Maintain and organize regulatory and compliance documents, reports, and other metrics using electronic media Engage in service to the Clinical Mental Health program, the College of Health Sciences and Human Services, and the university Perform other related duties as assigned for the success of the program and division Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.  For full consideration, qualified applicants should submit the following: 1) letter of intent; 2) curriculum vitae; teaching and supervision philosophy statements; 4) concise statement about your approach to teaching or other initiatives designed to foster a sense of student engagement, community, and belonging; 5) transcripts; and 6) contact information for three references. For inquiries, contact Dr. Jeffry Thigpen, Head for the Division of Human Services ( jthigpen@methodist.edu ). All applications should be submitted through http://www.methodist.edu/positions-available . Qualifications Minimum Qualifications PhD from a CACREP accredited institution in Counselor Education and Supervision Minimum of three years of clinical experience Professional identity in the counseling profession Minimum of three years of higher education experience with successful teaching Licensure as a Licensed Clinical Mental Health Counselor or Licensed Professional Counselor or eligible to seek and gain licensure Preferred Qualifications Experience with teaching and curriculum development in an online graduate program in clinical mental health counseling Experience utilizing Lumivero Experiential Learning Cloud or similar online platforms for field experience coordination and documentation Leadership experience in program administration Experience with the CACREP accreditation standards and processes Experience supervising master’s level clinical mental health counseling students Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/161861": {
      "title": "Director of OT Admissions and Alumni Relations",
      "description": "Director of OT Admissions and Alumni Relations You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Director of OT Admissions and Alumni Relations Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description Director of OT Admissions and Alumni Relations Department of Occupational Therapy – Methodist University The Director of OT Admissions and Alumni Relations is a full-time staff position that provides administrative support to the Departmental Admissions Committees and their respective members. This professional plays an integral role in promoting Methodist University and both the Occupational Therapy Doctorate (OTD) and Occupational Therapy Assistant (OTA) programs through strategic recruitment marketing, digital content, and data-informed outreach. The Director is responsible for managing student recruitment and ensuring successful assimilation from candidacy to matriculation, as well as maintaining strong alumni engagement across both programs. Responsibilities Program Marketing and Student Recruitment Promote the university/programs and attract new students by maintaining working relationships with pipeline university departments/programs; collaborate closely with the alumni office and university relations department. Oversee and participate in the development of admissions materials, events, and marketing practices for both the OTD and OTA programs. Manage and participate in recruitment fairs and events both on and off campus. Manage and participate in promotional events, information sessions, campus tours, student interviews, and other admissions activities. Serve as the OT department's primary liaison to the university's marketing and communications office, ensuring recruitment materials and messaging follow institutional branding standards. Demonstrate a proficient understanding of the occupational therapy profession; effectively communicate the scope of practice, purpose, and professional opportunities of both programs to prospective students, families, and community members. Establish and expand professional awareness and recruit prospective students at the elementary school, middle school, high school, and undergraduate levels. Promote university and program initiatives focused on inclusivity, diversity, and the recruitment of non-traditional students. Digital Content and Marketing Strategy Develop and maintain a content calendar for OT program social media channels (e.g., Instagram, Facebook, LinkedIn), capturing student life, clinical experiences, and program milestones. Create and edit photography, short-form video, and graphics to support recruitment campaigns, in coordination with university marketing and communications standards. Maintain and update OT program webpages to ensure content is accurate, current, and optimized for prospective student search behavior. Design and distribute email marketing campaigns and newsletters targeted to prospective students at each stage of the admissions funnel. Coordinate with the university marketing and communications office on branding standards, promotional materials, and cross-platform outreach. Data-Driven Recruitment and CRM Management Manage prospective student data and communication workflows within OTCAS/WebAdMIT and any supplementary recruitment or CRM tools, ensuring accurate tracking from initial inquiry through matriculation. Build and maintain targeted, automated follow-up and nurture communications to move prospective students through the admissions pipeline. Track recruitment and marketing metrics, including inquiry-to-application conversion, lead source, and yield, to inform outreach strategy. Analyze the effectiveness of recruitment marketing campaigns and adjust strategy based on results. Prepare regular recruitment and marketing analytics reports for the Program Director/Chair and Admissions Committee. Development of Admission and Retention Strategies Establish comprehensive admission processes to maintain a continual flow of quality applicants and transfers to the university by analyzing enrollment trends and marketing effectiveness. Coordinate systematic and efficient application management and ensure effective communication with applicants. Explain admission guidelines, processes, and requirements. Effectively utilize the centralized application system as a consistent platform for student information and a resource to track outstanding admission requirements. Manage the admissions process from initial contact through student onboarding and registration for both the OTD and OTA programs: Conduct information sessions and campus tours Perform transcript reviews Organize and score applications Plan and execute admission interview events Create and maintain applicant files, including application scores, admissions requirements, enrollment forms, deposit records, and enrollment documentation for incoming students. Plan and oversee new student orientation for both programs. Manage the ordering, purchasing, and distribution of new student materials such as name tags, uniform shirts, equipment kits, parking passes, anatomy lab locks, etc. Maintain student records in Ellucian. Alumni Relations Develop, implement, and manage effective alumni relations and required data collection processes for both the OTD and OTA programs, including graduate status, employment, and contact information. Develop and maintain a bi-annual newsletter to ensure ongoing communication with alumni, including professional accomplishments, program updates, and university events. Assist in the planning and preparation for the annual alumni event hosted by the OT department. Formulate a comprehensive bi-annual statistical report of graduate data as required by the Program Director, the university, and/or accreditation bodies. Meet monthly with the OT Department Chair and Chair of the Admissions Committee. Qualifications Qualifications Education Bachelor's degree required. Degree in Marketing, Communications, Higher Education, Business, or a related field preferred. Professional Experience Three (3) years of experience in higher education admissions, student recruitment, enrollment management, or marketing/communications; experience within a health professions or graduate program setting preferred. Experience developing and executing digital marketing or content campaigns (social media, email, web) preferred. Preferred Qualifications Experience with OTCAS/WebAdMIT or similar centralized application systems. Experience with CRM platforms (e.g., Ellucian, Slate) for recruitment tracking, reporting, and communication. Demonstrated skill in social media management and short-form video/photo content creation, and working familiarity with basic graphic design tools (e.g., Adobe Creative Cloud, Canva). Experience analyzing recruitment and marketing data to inform strategy and reporting to leadership. Knowledge of occupational therapy education or ACOTE accreditation requirements. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to represent the program to prospective students, families, faculty, and community partners. Ability to manage multiple projects and deadlines independently in a fast-paced admissions cycle. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail in application review, data management, and reporting. Ability to travel regionally for recruitment events, including occasional evenings and weekends during peak recruitment seasons. Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/161163": {
      "title": "Open Rank Faculty of Engineering",
      "description": "Open Rank Faculty of Engineering You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Open Rank Faculty of Engineering Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Faculty Apply Description The Department of Engineering in the Division of Engineering and Environmental invites applications for a tenure track position as Assistant/Associate Professor. The department seeks a candidate with teaching experience in industrial and systems engineering – specifically statistics and operations research, as well as the ability to supervise undergraduate student research . Candidates with backgrounds in all areas of industrial and systems engineering are encouraged to apply. Preference will be given to those with expertise in operations research, statistics, data analytics, and engineering management. Candidates should possess the ability to teach a variety of undergraduate engineering and industrial engineering classes, including Probability and statistics, Operations research, Engineering management, Engineering economy, and Data mining/analytics. Faculty members are expected to teach in the Methodist University engineering curriculum, mentor students, and participate in institutional service and the academic governance of the department, college, and university. Additionally, faculty members are encourage to develop and maintain research projects involving undergraduate students. We seek candidates whose teaching, research, and/or service has prepared them to address engineering in the context of social responsibility, support departmental efforts to improve student career readiness, and add to ongoing efforts to increase the preparation, retention, and persistence of students in STEM. Academic rank and salary are commensurate with level of education as well as professional and academic experience. Candidates should be interested in curriculum design and assessment. Application Materials: Candidates will initially submit the following: (1) cover letter summarizing interests and qualifications; (2) curriculum vitae; (3) teaching philosophy statement; (4) concise statement about your approach to teaching or other initiatives designed to foster a sense of student engagement, community, and belonging; (5) contact information for three references. Application review will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. This position is conditional based upon budgetary approval. Anticipated start date is as early as January 2027. For inquiries, contact Dr. Densie Bauer ( dbauer@methodist.edu ), Engineering Program Director and Head of the Engineering and Environmental Studies Division. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Industrial Engineering, Industrial and Systems Engineering, or a closely related field by the start date. ABD candidates may be considered. Teaching experience in the areas of operations research, statistics, and/or data analytics. Commitment to inclusive pedagogy and teaching excellence. Ability to teach Operations Research, Engineering Economy, Engineering Probability and Statistics, Data Mining, and Data Analytics. Ability to guide and mentor student research in engineering-based projects. Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/161009": {
      "title": "Open Rank Faculty Occupational Therapy Assistant (BS-OTA) Program",
      "description": "Open Rank Faculty Occupational Therapy Assistant (BS-OTA) Program You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Open Rank Faculty Occupational Therapy Assistant (BS-OTA) Program Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Faculty Apply Description Summary Methodist University, located in Fayetteville, NC, is seeking a 9-month, full-time, open rank BS-OTA faculty member.  Methodist University Occupational Therapy Assistant Program is a Bachelor of Science program. Academic rank and salary are commensurate with level of education as well as professional and academic experience.  We are seeking applicants passionate about teaching who can add to our team approach to occupational therapy education.  In addition to faculty responsibilities (teaching, scholarship, service) this faculty position will serve as the Coordinator for the BS-OTA Baccalaureate Project. This is a full-time, tenure track position that requires day and occasional evening & weekend availability. Position Description OTA faculty are responsible for leveraging their expertise to develop, maintain and deliver core education courses to students through: Preparing course plans, materials, and student assessment methods Delivering course instruction & student evaluation Monitoring academic, clinical skill, and professional behavior progress Facilitating interprofessional and intraprofessional learning activities Advising students Support and mentor students in the development, implementation, and evaluation of baccalaureate project Maintain policies, curriculum, and assessment of baccalaureate project for the BS-OTA Program Contribute to accreditation reporting Establishing and maintaining ongoing professional scholarship and development Maintaining a record of department, university, and community service Other duties: Attend all faculty and departmental meetings. Participation in the selection of applicants for admission to the program Attendance of educational conferences and workshops. Participation in state and national OT associations, leadership positions are encouraged. Other duties as assigned by the dean or department chair. Applications Applications will be accepted until the position is filled.  Qualified candidates are invited to submit a letter of intent, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy statement, and concise statement about teaching or other experiences, successes, and challenges in working with a diverse student population.  All applications should be submitted through http://www.methodist.edu/positions-available .  For questions, contact Melissa Gibson, OTA Program Director at megibson@methodist.edu . Qualifications Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree required May be initially certified OT or OTA practitioner A current, unrestricted North Carolina OT or OTA license (or eligible) At least 2 years of clinical practice in the field of occupational therapy Preferred Qualifications Familiarity with ACOTE Standards and the accreditation processes. Demonstrated knowledge of practice settings across the lifespan. Ability to support and mentor students in the development, implementation, and evaluation of project-based work involving diverse populations, community needs, and emerging practice areas. Strong understanding of evidence-based practice, scholarly inquiry, and project development Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/160896": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Medical Education and Biomedical Sciences Faculty, School of Medicine",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Medical Education and Biomedical Sciences Faculty, School of Medicine You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Professor, Medical Education and Biomedical Sciences Faculty, School of Medicine School of Medicine Location - Fayetteville, NC 28304 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Faculty Apply Description Methodist University Cape Fear Valley Health School of Medicine, located in the vibrant and diverse community of Fayetteville, NC, is poised for growth and innovation with preliminary LCME accreditation. We are seeking visionary medical educators in the fields of Microbiology, Anatomical Sciences including Neuroanatomy, and Histopathology to join our growing team and help shape the future of medical education. Are you a creative, forward-thinking, and student-focused educator ? Do you thrive on innovation and the opportunity to influence the next generation of physician leaders? Join our Department of Medical Education and Biomedical Sciences as we design and deliver a cutting-edge, spirally integrated, clinical presentation curriculum. Why Join Us? Our mission is bold yet vital: to prepare graduates to become socially accountable, equity-focused, community-engaged physician leaders committed to reducing health disparities and improving outcomes in southeastern North Carolina and beyond. What You’ll Do: Teach and mentor future physicians through large and small group facilitation , including case-based learning based on clinical presentations . Develop and implement an innovative curriculum grounded in the latest educational methodologies. Design, develop, and direct an assigned course as a course director and contribute to other courses as a discipline/thread expert. Collaborate with all faculty to build courses/clerkships for the program Contribute to educational scholarship Participate in educational service and academic citizenship Mentor students What We’re Looking For: Expertise in Microbiology, Anatomical Sciences, including Neuroanatomy, and Histopathology gained through the attainment of a terminal degree (e.g., PhD or equivalent degree). Medical school teaching experience and small group facilitation. A commitment to fostering a culture of innovation, collaboration, and excellence in medical education. What We Offer: The opportunity to play a pivotal role in shaping a new medical school . A supportive and inclusive academic culture that values equity, community engagement, and professional growth . The chance to work in a community-focused environment addressing real-world healthcare challenges . Competitive compensation in a family-friendly affordable community nestled between the North Carolina coast and the research triangle community. Be part of a mission-driven team dedicated to transforming medical education and empowering future physicians to make meaningful change in their communities. Apply Today! Visit the Methodist University Careers Page to join us in this exciting journey toward educational innovation and social impact. Qualifications What We’re Looking For: Expertise in Microbiology, Anatomical Sciences, including Neuroanatomy, and Histopathology gained through the attainment of a terminal degree (e.g., PhD or equivalent degree). Medical school teaching experience and small group facilitation. A commitment to fostering a culture of innovation, collaboration, and excellence in medical education. Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/159631": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Business Administration",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor of Business Administration You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Instructor of Business Administration Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Apply Description Position Type Adjunct Faculty Description The Reeves School of Business at Methodist University is seeking qualified adjunct faculty to teach undergraduate courses in Business Administration. Teaching opportunities may include introductory and upper-level courses in areas such as Principles of Management, Principles of Marketing, Business Communications, Organizational Behavior, Human Resource Management, Business Ethics, Strategic Management, Entrepreneurship, Business Law, and other business disciplines based on departmental needs. We are seeking instructors with experience teaching in face-to-face, hybrid, and online asynchronous modalities who are committed to student success and engaged learning. Requirements Interested applicants should submit: Letter of interest Curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy (not to exceed one page) Statement describing your approach to fostering student engagement, community, and belonging in the classroom (not to exceed one page) Questions regarding this position may be directed to the Dean of the Reeves School of Business at Methodist University. Qualifications Qualifications A master's degree in Business Administration or a closely related business discipline from a regionally accredited institution is required. Candidates must possess a minimum of eighteen (18) graduate semester credit hours in the discipline they are qualified to teach, consistent with SACSCOC faculty credentialing guidelines. Preference will be given to applicants with college-level teaching experience and/or significant professional experience in business or industry. Successful completion of a criminal history records check is required. Methodist University reserves the right to authenticate academic and professional credentials and to consult public records prior to extending offers of employment. Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/159458": {
      "title": "Open Rank Nursing Faculty",
      "description": "Open Rank Nursing Faculty You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Open Rank Nursing Faculty Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Faculty Apply Description Department: Department of Nursing, College of Health Sciences and Human Services Reports To: Nursing School Head Appointment: Full-time, 9-month faculty appointment. Rank and tenure eligibility determined by qualifications and experience. Position Summary Methodist University invites applications for a full-time nursing faculty position in the pre-licensure Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) program. The successful candidate will teach didactic, laboratory, and clinical courses across the undergraduate curriculum. This position is ideal for a nurse educator with a strong generalist foundation who is committed to preparing practice-ready graduates for licensure and professional practice. Essential Responsibilities Teach assigned didactic, simulation, laboratory, and clinical courses in the pre-licensure BSN program, with emphasis on fundamentals, adult health, medical-surgical, and critical care content Supervise students in acute care clinical settings and maintain effective working relationships with clinical partners Participate in curriculum development, course revision, and program assessment activities aligned with CCNE accreditation standards and North Carolina Board of Nursing requirements Mentor undergraduate nursing students, including support for NCLEX-RN preparation and success Contribute to student recruitment, admission, and progression processes, as assigned Engage in scholarship consistent with rank and university expectations Serve on department, college, and university committees Participate in interprofessional education initiatives within the College of Health Sciences and Human Services Maintain current clinical competence and licensure Application Materials Applicants should submit a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and contact information for three professional references. Qualifications Required Qualifications Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) from an accredited program Current unencumbered RN license in North Carolina or eligibility for licensure prior to start date Minimum of two years of clinical experience in adult health, medical-surgical, or critical care nursing Demonstrated ability to teach and evaluate students in classroom and clinical settings Commitment to student-centered teaching and inclusive learning environments Preferred Qualifications Earned doctorate in nursing or related field (PhD, DNP, or EdD); ABD candidates with a defined completion timeline will be considered Prior teaching experience in a pre-licensure nursing program Certification in a relevant specialty (e.g., CCRN, CMSRN, PCCN) or nursing education (CNE) Experience with simulation-based education Record of scholarship, professional service, or clinical leadership appropriate to rank Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/157839": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Biology",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor of Biology You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Instructor of Biology Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Adjunct Faculty Apply Description The Division of Natural Science at Methodist University is seeking adjunct faculty to teach lower-division courses (lecture with lab) in Biology. Our recurring needs include Fundamentals of Biology I and Biological Science (for non-majors). We are looking for instructors with experience teaching face-to-face and online asynchronous modalities. Requirements : Interested persons should submit a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy statement (no more than 1-page in length), and a statement that articulates their approach to teaching or other initiatives designed to foster a sense of student engagement, community, and belonging (not to exceed 1-page in length). Please address any questions to Dr. Vijay Antharam, Division Head of Natural Science (vantharam@methodist.edu). Qualifications A Master’s Degree in Biology, or closely related discipline from a regionally accredited institution. Eighteen (18) credit hours in Biology at the graduate level is required. Teaching experience and/or more than one year of relevant field experience are a plus. Successful completion of a criminal history records check. Methodist University reserves the right to authenticate academic and professional credentials and to consult public records prior to extending offers of employment. Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/156740": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Social Work",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor of Social Work You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Instructor of Social Work Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Adjunct Faculty Apply Description The Department of Social Work at Methodist University is seeking adjunct faculty to teach courses in its Bachelor of Social Work program beginning August 2026.  Embedded within the Division of Human Services in the College of Health Sciences and Human Services, the BSW program prepares students for generalist social work practice with individuals, families, groups, organizations, and communities.  The program is accredited by the Council on Social Work Education (CSWE) and highly regarded in the state of North Carolina and beyond.  Adjunct instructors are responsible for teaching online and/or in a traditional classroom setting in curricular areas related to social work practice methods, human behavior and the social environment, and social welfare policy. Interested persons should submit a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy statement (no more than 1-page in length), and a statement that articulates their approach to teaching or other initiatives designed to foster a sense of student engagement, community, and belonging (not to exceed 1-page in length).  The letter of interest should identify the area(s) of the curriculum you are interested in teaching in along with an explanation of your qualifications to teach courses in that area(s). Qualifications MSW degree from a CSWE-accredited program (DSW or PhD in Social Work preferred) 2-years, full-time post-MSW practice experience Experience teaching undergraduate or graduate social work courses Experience with Canvas Learning Management System Availability to teach in person and/or online Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/154147": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor for Industrial and Systems Engineering",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor for Industrial and Systems Engineering You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Instructor for Industrial and Systems Engineering Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Adjunct Faculty Apply Description The Division of Engineering and Environmental Studies is seeking applications for an adjunct instructor in Industrial and Systems Engineering. Courses to be taught may include Operations Research Engineering Economy Data Analytics Engineering Probability and Statistics Engineering Management Design of Experiments We seek instructors who are adept in student-centered teaching methods, equity-based approaches to pedagogy and experience with digital teaching technologies. Responsibilities: Teach a M/W/F or T/TH on-campus schedule; however, hybrid or online options may be available based on experience and need. Course schedules may include up to 3 courses per semester. Course preparation, delivery, grading, and records management for each course for the full duration of scheduled instruction. Be fully prepared for each class session and enforce academic policy and procedures Comply with institutional rules and regulations. Maintain complete course and student records. To apply for this part-time position, submit the following materials CV/resume Cover letter Unofficial transcripts (showing 18 credit hours in field) and/or certification information Three references Contact Division Head, Dr. Denise Bauer at dbauer@methodist.edu with any questions. Qualifications Minimum qualifications: Bachelor’s in Industrial and Systems Engineering or closely related field and a minimum of 7 years of professional experience with a Professional Engineering license; OR Master’s degree with at least 18 graduate semester hours in Industrial and Systems Engineering or closely related field. Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/154045": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor for Environmental Health and Safety",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor for Environmental Health and Safety You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Instructor for Environmental Health and Safety Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Adjunct Faculty Apply Description The Division of Engineering and Environmental Studies is seeking applications for an adjunct instructor in Environmental Health and Safety. Courses to be taught may include OSHA Regulations for General Industry OSHA Regulations for Construction Environmental Audits and Assessments Industrial Hygiene and Toxicology Emergency Planning and Preparedness. We seek instructors who are adept in student-centered teaching methods, equity-based approaches to pedagogy and experience with digital teaching technologies. Responsibilities: Teach a M/W/F or T/TH on-campus schedule; however, hybrid or online options may be available based on experience and need. Course schedules may include up to 3 courses per semester. Course preparation, delivery, grading, and records management for each course for the full duration of scheduled instruction. Be fully prepared for each class session and enforce academic policy and procedures Comply with institutional rules and regulations. Maintain complete course and student records. To apply for this part-time position, submit the following materials CV/resume Cover letter Unofficial transcripts (showing 18 credit hours in field) and/or certification information Three references Contact Division Head, Dr. Denise Bauer at dbauer@methodist.edu with any questions. Qualifications Minimum qualifications: Bachelor’s in Environmental or Occupational Health & Safety, Environmental Science, Engineering, or closely related field and a minimum of 5 years of Environmental Health and Safety experience with a Safety Professional and/or Industrial Hygienist certification; OR Master’s degree with at least 18 graduate semester hours in Occupational Health and Safety, Environmental Science, or closely related field. Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
