    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/151850": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor in Art and Graphic Design",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor in Art and Graphic Design You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Instructor in Art and Graphic Design Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Adjunct Faculty Apply Description The Division of Fine and Performing Arts at Methodist University seeks Adjunct Instructors in Art and Graphic Design. Courses and topics may include: Graphic Design Studio Typography Interactive Design Language of Art Business and Marketing in Art Photographic Media Art History and Theory Foundations: Drawing and Painting Applications Qualified candidates are invited to submit a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, three references, and a 1–2-page Teaching Philosophy. Candidates are also invited to submit a link to a portfolio or example works. Qualifications All successful candidates will have a Master’s Degree in Art or Graphic Design, experience teaching in any of the above areas, and be proficient in the Adobe Creative Suite programs – specifically, Photoshop, Illustrator, and InDesign. Adjunct instructors may teach between one and three courses per semester; each course is three credit hours, although some may require more contact time. Preference will be given to those with graphic design and photography teaching experience. Industry experience will also be considered. Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/150224": {
      "title": "Custodian - Temporary (Summer 2026)",
      "description": "Custodian - Temporary (Summer 2026) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Custodian - Temporary (Summer 2026) Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Part Time/Temporary Apply Description This job posting is for a part-time, temporary position, during the summer, starting in May 2026 and ending in August 2026.  Specific dates will be identified during the recruitment process. Serves as a custodial team member responsible for the cleanliness of facilities that influence image and perception of the University. Follows directives of the custodial supervisors or housekeeping department officials responsible for the coordination and accomplishment of facility housekeeping operations or under the direct supervision of employees in a higher classification; perform duties in accordance with established standards and instruction. Although this is an entry-level position, the role requires a high level of commitment and pride in work being performed. The daily activities include but are not limited to: following 7-step cleaning methods, adjusting cleaning techniques to meet the cleanliness standard, changing assignments, and interacting with teammates, students, staff and faculty professional. TYPICAL JOB DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES 1. Sweep, mop and scrub floors, stairs (interior) and other surfaces. 2. Use light (industrial type) floor machines and attachments. 3. Vacuum rugs in offices and public areas. 4. Clean and dust furniture, exhibit cases, pictures, door trim and chalk/white boards. 5. Wash window sills, glass in corridor doors, glass countertops, etc. 6. Wash glass and trim in entrance doors. 7. Wash and/or clean interior wall spaces by hand or with powered wall washing machine, working on ladders and scaffolding, as required. 8. Clean and service lavatories, toilet rooms and rest rooms. 9. Collect and place in containers or plastic bags trash and debris, place trash in collection area for removal by grounds team or designated personnel. 10. Replace liners in wastebaskets and trash containers. 11. Move/shift heavy (50lbs or less) furniture, supplies and miscellaneous equipment, as directed. 12. Report items that need repair (doors, door checks, furniture lights, faucets, etc.) 13. Respond to/remedy emergent/intermittent requests, i.e. water/plumbing issues, mold/mildew remediation using special equipment and products 14. Prepare venues for campus events, i.e. restrooms, auditorium, gymnasium, student center, seasonal athletics, academic facilities, etc. 15. Perform related duties, as assigned. PHYSICAL DEMANDS AND WORKING CONDITIONS Transporting moderately heavy items, at times, to and from labs. Qualifications EDUCATION/EXPERIENCE: High School/GED or the equivalent required. Any combination of experience and training that would likely provide the required knowledge and abilities is qualifying. Cleaning in an institutional environment is a plus. Applicant must be able to furnish work/character references. KNOWLEDGE OF: Cleaning methods, materials and equipment Hazards and safety precautions related to general maintenance and custodial activities. ABILITY TO: To comprehend and implement techniques provided through training sessions and/or feedback from department leadership. Clean and care for assigned areas and equipment. Read and write English to carry out oral and written directions. Establish and maintain effective working relationships with those contacted in the course of work. Communicate effectively, both orally and in writing. Lift/move heavy cleaning equipment. Work weekends in addition to regular work week based on university activities and cleaning requirements. It is a condition of employment. Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/148457": {
      "title": "Clinical Adjunct Nurse Faculty",
      "description": "Clinical Adjunct Nurse Faculty You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Clinical Adjunct Nurse Faculty Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Adjunct Faculty Apply Description The purpose of the Clinical Nursing Instructor is to supplement the classroom experience by teaching and supervising pre-licensure BSN nursing students in the clinical agency. Clinical Nurse Faculty report to the BSN Program Director with supervision from the Clinical Coordinator and Course Coordinators for the assigned subject area. Subject areas may include Mental Health/Psychiatric Nursing, Medical/Surgical Nursing, Community/ Public Health Nursing, and Obstetrics/Pediatric Nursing. Adjunct Nurse Faculty are generally appointed at the rank of Instructor. General Roles and Responsibilities include: Making patient/student assignments Providing clinical instruction Assessing each student's progress and providing verbal and/or written feedback to the student Completing a formal, summative evaluation of the student's clinical performance using the clinical evaluation tool developed for the course Adhere to the policies and procedures of the clinical site Qualifications Minimum requirements for these positions include: A Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) and previous experience teaching clinical in a Registered Nursing or higher program is preferred. All candidates will hold a minimum of a Bachelor of Science in Nursing degree (BSN) from an accredited institution of higher education. Have two calendar years or the equivalent of full-time clinical experience as a registered nurse. Hold a current unrestricted license or multistate licensure privilege to practice as a registered nurse in North Carolina. Have preparation in teaching and learning principles for adult education or the ability and willingness to complete the North Carolina Board of Nursing teaching/learning requirements within three years of hire. Maintain competence in the areas of assigned responsibility; Have current knowledge of nursing practice for the registered nurse. Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/24375BA29C8AE0EA98AC3A9FD8D2FDCE/jobs/146710": {
      "title": "Assistant Football Coach",
      "description": "Assistant Football Coach You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Football Coach Methodist University Location - Fayetteville, NC 28311 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description Assistant Football Coach – Methodist University (NC) DIII Methodist University is accepting applications for Assistant Football Coach (Quarterbacks). Responsibilities include providing academic support for our student athletes through our One Stop, and assisting the head coach in all aspects of recruiting, retention, and implementing best practices for our football program in accordance with NCAA, USA South Conference and Methodist University guidelines, regulations, and philosophies. Applications will be reviewed immediately upon arrival and continue until the position is filled.  Methodist University in harmony with its tradition takes seriously the ethical and moral development of students…Methodist University reserves the right to authenticate academic and professional credentials and consult public records prior to extending offers of employment.  EOE Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree required, Master’s Degree preferred…successful coaching experience (Previous Coordinator experience preferred) with demonstrated experience in the recruitment and retention of student-athletes at the NCAA III level preferred. Possession of a valid drivers license and ability to meet all university requirements for operating a university-owned or leased vehicle, including successfully completing the motor vehicle record (MVR) check and maintaining an acceptable driving record throughout employment. Send letter of application, resume and contact information on three professional references to: kgwilliams@methodist.edu Share job details to About METHODIST UNIVERSITY INC Introduction to Methodist University Methodist University - Engage. Enrich. Empower. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. 